WEBVTT

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.110
This is so dumb.

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:04.520
Do what you like!

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.270
Urabe Hayato

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.900
I'm quitting the Dolphins, anyway, 
so it's none of my business anymore!

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.190
Resignation

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.890
<i>Even though his dream match
with Touto is days away,</i>

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.450
<i>Urabe's said he's quitting the team.</i>

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.120
He's a lost cause.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.970
Andy!

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:24.210
Suzuki Andy

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.620
I tried to talk some sense into him,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.800
but he's so done with baseball, 
he won't listen to anything I say.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.710
I guess losing his spot as starting pitcher 
for the Touto match really got to him.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.460
Sakura Mutsuko

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.460
I suppose it would, yeah.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.300
I <i>need </i>to win two more games
so we can play the Touto Boys!

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:39.080
Urabe-kun's worked so hard to get 
himself into a position to beat Touto.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.310
Looks like we're gonna have to rely on Satou.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:49.770
Urabe... Are you really 
gonna just quit like this?!

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:28.000
Before the Big Game

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Resignation

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.610
I'm not trying to defend him, 
but he's had it rough.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:36.740
Huh?

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.490
He used to be a small, sickly child,

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.650
so his father got him into baseball.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.080
His father played junior baseball way back
and even made it to Nationals,

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.710
and he put Urabe on a harsh individual 
training regimen from an early age.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:58.850
With a stronger body, and armed 
with a wealth of baseball knowledge,

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.700
Urabe joined the Touto Boys, full of hope.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.670
That's where he met Mayumura Wataru.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.390
Mayumura was the son of a major leaguer,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.250
but until he joined the team, 
he'd pretty much played zero baseball.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.370
In the beginning, he was 
utterly unremarkable,

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.630
but in no time, he became a formidable player.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.130
Since he was really athletic, 
quick on the uptake,

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:25.890
and a lefty, the manager 
told him he should try pitching.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.360
By the time fall came around in fourth grade,

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.410
he'd already surpassed Urabe and was on 
the same level as the seasoned pitchers.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.400
Then, that means...

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:40.280
Yes, Urabe's spot was taken by the
 offspring of a pro. Sound familiar?

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:47.300
That's why Urabe was so hostile 
to you guys in the beginning.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.890
We'd love to see what kind of skills 
thoroughbreds like you are packing!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.220
Having the DNA of a pro 
gives you such a huge advantage

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:00.690
over regular kids who have been 
training hard since they were small.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.750
Well, that's not true for <i>every</i> child of a pro...

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.040
Aha! You went there!

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.310
You burned me good, bro!

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:14.270
After all that, when he heard he wasn't
starting the Touto game as pitcher,

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.020
the fight went out of him.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:20.820
Resignation

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.590
I told him it was no reason to quit,

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:25.510
but he said he'd just drag the team down
if he was just going through the motions.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.560
He went as far as saying that, huh?

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.170
Isn't there anything we can
say to make him reconsider?

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.240
No, it's no use.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.290
He's made the decision to quit on his own.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.520
On his own, you say?

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.130
I've just come up with a great idea!

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.130
I'm home.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.280
Hayato, your friend is here.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.330
It's hot down here, so I told him 
he could wait for you in your room.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:05:01.110
Oh, and you accidentally threw this 
in the trashcan, so I washed it for you.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.610
"Friend"?

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:05.910
Who...

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.310
Sh-Shigeno?!

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.530
Heya! This idol magazine's a good read!

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.160
This is the girl you're into, right?

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:16.120
You have her as your
phone wallpaper, dontcha?

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.720
Her hairstyle and stuff
sorta remind me of my sister...

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.220
What the hell are you doing in my house?!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.120
If you're trying to make me
reconsider quitting, I'm not listening!

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:28.510
Please, hear me out!

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.510
I don't care what you do or say, 
I won't change my mind!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.200
But just listen to what Sakura-san said...

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.360
"If Urabe-kun quits, I'm going to cry!"

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.230
"We swore we'd defeat
Touto together. Boohoo."

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:46.790
You dipwad! She doesn't 
give a rat's ass about Touto!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.130
Wh-What about Andy, then?

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.330
"Urabe, come back.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.120
You and I go way back, don't we?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.180
I am Andy."

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.330
Stop doing weird impressions! 
Andy doesn't talk like that!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.890
Anyway, trying to persuade me 
to reconsider is pointless!

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:04.900
All right. I'll stop trying to persuade you.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:15.720
Resignation

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:10.120
We decided we'd all quit 
if you quit the team, anyway.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.190
After all, without you, 
we have no hope of winning.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:15.600
Andy and Sakura-san have 
both lost their motivation, too.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:16.790
What?!

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:20.090
Let's take them all to the manager tomorrow.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:22.180
We'll have to forfeit the Touto game...

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.250
I see.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.240
Huh?

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.650
Just quit if you want to! 
It has nothing to do with me!

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.240
B-But...

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.290
Now, get the hell out!

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.000
Your plan failed?!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:45.250
I tried to tug at his heartstrings by saying 
we'd all quit if he quit, but it didn't work.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.260
Resignation

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:47.920
He didn't even blink when I said it.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.440
Sounds like him.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.950
He's just a hopeless case.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:57.050
But you know, he still hasn't handed 
in his resignation letter, has he?

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:57.640
Huh?

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.910
Maybe he still has some doubts in his mind.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.360
Perhaps he just wants attention.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:12.920
Hey!

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:16.540
What do <i>you</i> want? I'm not changing my mind.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.370
I'm about to go hand my 
resignation in to the manager.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.000
It's not about that.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:24.500
I need to talk to you about something.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.780
If Urabe quits, I won't have 
anyone to practice my bunting with.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:34.970
So you're going to ask me to help you?

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.580
You guessed right! You're so smart!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:40.450
Would you practice with me like 
last time, Sakura-san? Pretty please!

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:44.440
Sorry, I can't today. I've got cram school.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.820
What? No way!

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.030
Bye.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.730
What, seriously?

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.950
Now, I don't even have 
anyone to play catch with.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:54.210
Well, in that case...

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.450
Yamamuro Grade School

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.450
You want me to be your 
batting practice pitcher?!

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:01.040
Please! I've run out of people to ask!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.830
Katsumata

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.830
Matsubara

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.830
Nagai

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.830
B-But... why don't you just ask Urabe-kun?

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:09.160
Well, because he's quitting the team.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:09.820
What?!

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:10.810
Seriously?!

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:12.050
Urabe's quitting?

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:16.550
N-No way. Can we even beat Touto without him?

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.270
I don't know, but we have 
to at least practice, right?

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.850
I see.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:26.480
Sorry, man. We already 
made plans to go play games

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.400
with Kimura-kun and Ariyoshi-kun.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.430
Huh?

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:32.240
What's more important? Games or baseball?!

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.860
We made these plans a long 
time ago. We can't just cancel.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.140
Oh, well, all right.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:42.120
Fine. I'll go ask my sister to help me out.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:51.110
Daigo-kun's a lot more enthusiastic about 
practicing than he was before, isn't he?

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:54.320
He's really improved as an
outfielder and as a catcher, too.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:57.240
Hey, should we get in 
touch with the other guys?

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:01.470
If Urabe-kun really is quitting, this might 
not be the best time to be playing games.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.110
Yeah! Let's head down to 
the batting cages, Nagai!

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.380
After all, you could do with 
working on your hitting.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:09.180
Shut up. I'm not coming.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:13.530
Even if Urabe quits, the outfield 
positions aren't gonna just open up.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:18.470
Besides, I kinda get what 
Urabe's going through.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.410
See ya.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.830
<i>Oh, man...</i>

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.570
<i>I can't ask my sister to practice 
with me every day, either.</i>

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:29.690
Shigeno!

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.840
U-Urabe!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.080
What the...

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.680
Just so you know, I haven't
 changed my mind about quitting.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:38.640
Huh?

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.120
Andy's been pestering me non-stop.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.030
He said he won't try to stop me from quitting,

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.430
but he insisted I help you 
as your batting practice pitcher.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.190
Really? That'd be awesome!

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:51.550
I don't particularly <i>want </i>to 
help out the son of a pro, but...

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:53.480
I seriously appreciate it.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.620
But I figured you were 
a next gen failure, anyway, so...

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:11.890
You sure I should be standing this far over?

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:12.660
Yes!

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:18.540
When I picture where Mayumura-san's 
sidearm pitch angles in from,

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.280
it's near where you're standing now.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:26.020
Now, I just need my push bunt to hit 
this board with decent force.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.610
All right, I'm ready.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:33.110
Since I'm bunting for a base hit, 
I need to stand like I'm about to slug it.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:41.110
Oops! That wasn't good.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.510
What's going on here?

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:56.860
I already mastered sacrifice 
bunts on 100 kmph pitches...

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:58.760
I'll get this next one!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:09.010
Hey, dude, are you okay?

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.100
Is your nose still on?

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.620
I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.610
I just have to get used to the speed.

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:20.120
Can you really bunt for 
a base hit on this pitch?

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:22.700
Even a sacrifice bunt seems beyond you.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:25.980
<i>This is harder than I thought.</i>

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:30.200
<i>Maybe it's 'cause I'm rushing to switch 
from a hitting stance to a bunting stance?</i>

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.790
No, no, no, Daigo.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.880
What you're doing is a total waste of time.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.500
S-Sis!

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.890
What's with that outfit?

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:50.890
<i>Shigeno's older sister is </i>hella<i> cute!</i>

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:57.070
You were bragging before 
about your bunting skills.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.150
Is <i>this</i> what you were bragging about?

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:01.300
Huh? Well, I guess...

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.980
Didn't anyone teach you how to bunt?

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:05.410
Or are you self-taught?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:06.510
What?

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:09.500
I know how to bunt! I've been 
watching baseball since forever.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.160
I've pulled it off in games, too.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.290
That explains everything.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.230
Give me the bat.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:23.640
If you're facing a slow ball, you might just 
about manage with your self-taught bunt,

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:27.010
but it's obvious you 
can't handle faster balls.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.080
What's that kid's name?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.440
It's Urabe.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:33.480
Urabe-kun, can you pitch for me?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.610
S-Sure!

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:40.110
Pay close attention to how 
I use my arms and knees.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.620
Wow.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.960
So did you notice the difference?

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:58.790
Huh? You mean like how your butt got bigger?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.480
I'm talking about the bunt, you moron!

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:02.830
Ouchy-ouch-ouch.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:05.220
I'm sorry. I didn't notice any differences.

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:07.330
What am I gonna do with you?

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.910
Hang on a second.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.520
Here it is. The resistance band.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.020
What's that for?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.450
Okay! Now, try and do a bunt!

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.000
Huh? What's going on?

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.150
Is this your fetish?!

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:25.610
I call this special training technique:
 "The Banded Bunt!"

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.080
Wordplay? Really?

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.020
But I can't control my swing like this!

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:31.370
Urabe-kun, if you'd be so kind...

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.870
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.240
I can't bunt like this!

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.210
I can't even move my arms!

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.590
You don't bunt with your arms.
 You bunt with your legs!

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:45.620
What?

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:50.100
You're failing because you're only using
 your arms, which means you're all floppy.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:54.580
By pulling your arms in, you bring
 the bat closer to your body,

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.270
which makes it easier to see 
the ball on to the bat.

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:00.440
Placing the bat horizontal in 
front of your face at all times

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:05.420
and tracking the ball in the gap between bat
and eyes makes it easier to aim.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:09.730
Also, it's only your 
lower body that moves.

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:12.470
You adjust the height of 
the bat with your knees.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.920
For push bunts that require more force,

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.620
you create momentum 
by taking a step forward.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.410
If you don't even have these basics
of a sacrifice bunt down,

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.800
there's no way you can bunt for a hit.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:28.240
What?! Shut up! I'll show you!

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:32.030
Bunting is the only way I'll get 
a hit off Mayumura Michiru!

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:32.890
Urabe!

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:39.740
<i>Bring your arms in and lock 
the bat close to your body.</i>

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:44.400
<i>Keep the bat horizontal and track the ball
between the bat and your eyes.</i>

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:51.040
<i>Only move your lower body.</i>

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.230
Did you see that?

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.210
That's the Shigeno family DNA for you!

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:08.270
Or maybe it was my detailed 
instructions and the resistance band?

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:10.180
Don't start getting cocky.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:15.590
John Doe #28 needs to hit hundreds of those
before locking his arms becomes a habit.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:20.230
Oh, uh, miss? Are you taking a dip?

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:23.940
Hey, Shigeno! Instead of doing this crap,
we should jump in the pool, too!

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.170
What the heck are you talking about?

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.440
We don't have time to mess 
about before the big game!

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.450
That doesn't matter to me!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.450
<i>The Shigeno family DNA, huh?</i>

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.960
Fastballs

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.960
For both batting positions

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.960
Right-handed pitcher

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:48.250
I know we're doing this for practice, but...

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:52.050
Ariyoshi

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:52.050
Kishimoto

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:52.050
Kimura

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:51.020
These 120 kmph balls are just too hard to hit.

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:55.250
But if Urabe leaves, 
our offense will be weaker, too.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.220
You suck so bad!

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.520
Look at their bags! 
They're from the Nanyou Lions!

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.440
That well-known baseball powerhouse?

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:10.580
Mind you, we <i>are</i> fifth graders.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:15.370
There's no point in amateurs 
like you practicing hitting fastballs.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.240
Can you leave now? You're in our way.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:20.060
Didn't Nanyou reach the quarters?

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:24.790
W-Well, the mighty Dolphins 
made it to the quarterfinals, too.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.670
You lucked your way into 
the last eight, didn't you?

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.990
Don't you usually get 
knocked out in the first round?

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:33.380
Anyway, you guys will lose to Touto 
and crash out of the tournament.

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:34.300
Yeah.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:37.920
After we've won our next game, 
we'll be facing Touto.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.820
We need to get in and practice 
so we make the team.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.860
You're done in there, right?

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.350
Think you could just leave now?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.780
H-Hey!

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.800
We didn't say we were done!

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:51.620
Fine. Let's see how well <i>they</i> do.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.360
Fastballs

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.360
For both batting positions

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.360
Right-handed pitcher

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:00.410
You've gotta be kidding...

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.940
They're fifth graders?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.080
Shigeno

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.130
Shigeno, haven't you had enough?

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.980
How many more are you gonna make me throw?

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:22.720
I don't even throw this many 
when practicing with a catcher!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.630
You're right.

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:26.510
We should call it a day.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.020
We can pick it up again tomorrow.

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.440
What?! Tomorrow?!

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:31.460
What're you smo—

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.160
Urabe-kun's a pitcher, right?

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:36.450
And he's pitching in your game at the weekend?

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:39.820
You can't get in the way 
of his prep routine.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:44.270
Well, actually, he's resign—

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:46.280
It's fine, miss!

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:49.540
If it'll help Daigo-kun, I'll gladly 
come by tomorrow as well!

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.540
Really?

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:52.960
Are you sure, Urabe-kun?

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:56.120
Yes, it's all good. I'm not the 
starting pitcher, anyway.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:57.180
Anyway, see ya.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:58.930
Oh, Urabe-kun.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.780
Thank you.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:05.900
You throw some really good pitches.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:09.430
I see now how the Dolphins managed 
to get to the quarterfinals this season.

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:10.690
Huh?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.000
I figured it couldn't all be down 
to Hikaru-kun and Daigo,

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.240
whose training has been patchy,
to say the least.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.660
I-I didn't...

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:20.030
You guys won because there 
was someone on the team

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:22.830
who's been working hard year 
after year to get the basics down.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.200
Please lend Daigo and the others your 
strength in the Touto match, as well.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:45.560
Resignation

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:47.200
Thank you.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:50.080
You throw some really good pitches.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:53.310
I see now how the Dolphins managed 
to get to the quarterfinals this season.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:55.230
Resignation

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:58.510
Please lend Daigo and 
the others your strength.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:01.490
Resignation

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.500
Resignation

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:09.540
Urabe!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.660
Y-You guys?

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.280
Urabe-kun, Daigo-kun told us.

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:17.210
Are you really leaving the Dolphins?

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:21.480
Oh, it's just a misunderstanding.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:24.100
I made a joke and he took it seriously.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:26.350
Huh? But...

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:29.000
As if I'd quit in the middle
 of my final tournament!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.600
All I've gotta do now is put everything 
I've learned into the Touto match!

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.320
You guys need to get hits, too!

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:37.440
You can't rely on us to carry you forever!

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.740
We have to beat Touto, no matter what!

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.890
See ya!

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:46.250
So... he isn't quitting?

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:49.160
Whatever the case, he's totally right.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:54.840
We've only gotten this far because of 
Urabe-kun, Hikaru-kun, and Andy.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.010
It's not good enough.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.130
We need to become assets to the team.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.880
Yeah. Let's go to the batting 
center again tomorrow!

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:07.470
What?! Urabe-kun isn't quitting, after all?!

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:12.230
Yeah, I don't get it either. 
He called me out of the blue last night.

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:15.820
Please also tell your 
sister that I'll do my best!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.790
That's what he said.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:20.720
So he really <i>was</i> just 
looking for attention.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:24.240
Well, I'm just glad that he 
changed his mind in the end.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:33.150
Do you want me to help you train?

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:35.750
Thanks for the offer, Papa, but I'm okay.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:39.210
Satou Hikaru

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:39.040
It wouldn't be fair if I was the only one 
being coached by an ex-major leaguer.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:43.720
Besides, there's something Daigo-kun 
taught me that I want to try out.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.090
Satou Toshiya

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:45.550
I see.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.430
<i>Tomorrow's the big day.</i>

00:20:59.100 --> 00:21:01.300
<i>Good luck, Mr. Starting Pitcher.</i>

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:31.280
No good!

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:34.640
Mayumura Wataru

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:34.640
Touto Boys

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:34.640
Half a ball too high and 
a full ball's width too far in.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:37.370
What? You nitpick too much.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:40.150
Mayumura Michiru

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:40.150
Touto Boys

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:40.150
Who in the Dolphins could've even hit that?

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:41.980
Stop complaining.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.940
After we win tomorrow, we have 
the semifinals and the final on Sunday.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:47.940
If we're even half a ball off in 
those two games, we're done for.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:49.410
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:52.870
Mayumura Ken

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:58.280
Good morning!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:03.590
Everyone, time to celebrate! 
I've got good news!

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:05.300
What's that?

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:10.430
I thought they'd throw in their ace, 
but their starting pitcher isn't Mayumura!

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:13.310
Komatsu

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:13.310
Komatsu-kun?

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:14.680
Not their ace?

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:17.470
Does this mean they're underestimating us?

00:22:24.250 --> 00:22:25.610
<i>You're not going to pitch...</i>

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.510
<i>...Mayumura Michiru?</i>

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.670
So this is the powerhouse that is Touto Boys?!

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:06.320
Their starting pitcher's throwing 
some wicked fastballs,

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:08.260
and their offense has no weaknesses, either.

00:24:08.730 --> 00:24:10.260
The confidence of a champion.

00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:13.720
Or wait, do they think we're a joke?!

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:17.720
And then, on top of everything,
 Hikaru has an accident!

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
The Touto Match – Play Ball!

00:24:18.340 --> 00:24:21.450
Next time: "The Touto Match – Play Ball!"

00:24:21.450 --> 00:24:23.470
Run to the stage of your dreams!
